# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your RentCast key, then restart the Expo
# server (`npx expo start --clear`) — keys are read at build time, so a running
# server will not pick up edits to this file.
#
# The app only ever shows real API data. Without a key the Explore and Map
# screens say so instead of inventing houses.
#
# NOTE: anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is embedded in the JS bundle and is
# readable by anyone who installs the app. That is fine for a personal build,
# but do not ship this key in a public release.

# RentCast — property records with beds/baths/sqft/year built/last sale/owner.
# Sign up at https://www.rentcast.io/api, then create a key in the dashboard
# at https://app.rentcast.io/app/api
#
# Heads up: the free Developer plan includes only 50 requests per month, and
# the app fetches once per ~40m you walk. See README for how to stretch it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RENTCAST_API_KEY=
